From: Book4 Edge port
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: Add CameraSensorHelper for OmniVision OV02C10

The OV02C10 is the front sensor on the Samsung Galaxy Book4 Edge
(NP750XQA, Snapdragon X Plus), reached over CCI0 i2c0 at 0x36 and fed
into CAMSS through CSIPHY0.  libcamera has no helper for it, so the
soft ISP cannot map the sensor's analogue gain code to a real
multiplier and leaves AGC pinned at the minimum code.

Analogue gain is the usual OmniVision 4-bit fractional format.  From
drivers/media/i2c/ov02c10.c:

    #define OV02C10_ANAL_GAIN_MIN   0x10    /*  16 -> 1.0x  */
    #define OV02C10_ANAL_GAIN_MAX   0xf8    /* 248 -> 15.5x */

so code 0x10 is unity and the divisor is 16.

The black level target is programmed by the driver's mode register list
as 0x4002/0x4003 = 0x0040, i.e. 0x40 at 10 bits, matching the other
OmniVision helpers.

--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -678,6 +678,18 @@
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov01a10", CameraSensorHelperOv01a10)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperOv02c10 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperOv02c10()
+	{
+		/* From Linux kernel driver: 0x4002/0x4003 = 0x40 at 10bits. */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 16 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov02c10", CameraSensorHelperOv02c10)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperOv08x40 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
